            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "multilayered methanogenesis scheme",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "The multilayered methanogenesis scheme improves the representation of high-latitude CH4 emissions (previous studies underestimated production at cold permafrost sites during 'shoulder seasons')36. The multilayered scheme allows an insulated subsurface layer of active methanogenesis to continue after the surface has frozen. These model developments not only improve the seasonality of the emissions, but more importantly for this study capture the release of carbon as CH4 from deep soil layers, including thawed permafrost. The formulation of the multilayered scheme gives the local land-atmosphere CH4 flux, ECH4 (kgCm-2s-\u00b9), as",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
